# How the app works

Angular 9 gaming social app. Firebase project `greenhouse-e7063` (Auth, Firestore, Storage) is the only backend. NgRx handles auth, posts, and users. Source that produced this build is on `master` under `src/`; leave that branch alone.

- `/` → landing. Logged-in users go to `/post/list`.
- Login and Google sign-in set `localStorage.user` to `"logged"`, then load Firestore `users/{uid}`. Logout clears that key.
- Signed-in routes: `/post/list`, `/post/create`, `/post/:id`, `/user/list`, `/user/:id`.
- A post is title, description, and an image in Storage `/uploads/`. Comments are `posts/{id}/comments`. Likes are plain counters.
- User doc: `{ id, email, emailVerified, name, avatar }`.
